:[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101301","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101301.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101301.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"I propose that all strings that contain non-ascii characters must henceforth be marked as such (e.g. u8\"...\"), to catch accidental mistakes in string literals early. The check is performed by the static analyzer and takes only a few seconds: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/12676255818/job/35329065210?pr=101301\r\n\r\nThrough this test, I found one zero-width space in a string literal in `locales.h` (and another through explicit search in `CHANGELOG.md`.\r\n\r\nOther found instances were expected and could be safely marked as u8 literals.\r\n\r\nThis PR helps address https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100641.\r\nA better solution would be to set [-fexec-charset](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/cpp-oel-zos/2.0?topic=options-fexec-charset) to ASCII only, but unfortunately that does not seem to be supported right now.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101301/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101301/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}